-- tolosa.talk: owned by the Body TOLOSA (body-25), so `landed` delivered to
-- TOLOSA reaches this Script first. Landing trigger $38, arming $C0 (sticky:
-- it runs on every landing, never spent).

script variable visited = false     -- flag word bit 1 in the original

on landed body
  if not visited then
    put true into visited
    ask display to say "script56-inline-1"
    ask display to say "script56-inline-2"
  end if
  ask display to say "tolosa-attack"
  set the encounterGate of session to 1
  -- Bank word $070104. Native code reads it to arm the attack ship and to
  -- light the panel's second (red) lamp. A Host property shared with
  -- native code: exactly what `set` is for.
  -- ?? `session` here is a Host Object this Script didn't receive as an
  --    argument. It must be a well-known name the Host binds at Load
  --    (LoadOptions.objects?). talk.ts has no such option yet.
  epilogue
  -- ?? `epilogue` is a Handler in session.talk, not here. Calling it as a
  --    command sends it along THIS Script's Message Path (body-25 → session),
  --    which works, but it's a `send`, so it doesn't suspend this Run and
  --    the blank line races the next landing. The honest spelling is
  --    `send epilogue to session and wait`, or a shared module (Modules fog).
end landed
